0 !ACHILLES {"id":"ACH-Z01-S01","name":"Zone I · Scene 1: Hephaestus’s Forge & The Five-Fold Shield","zone":"Z01","lines":"18.468–482","greek":"Πρῶταคลὲν σάκος ποίει μέγα τε στιβαρόν τε πάντοσε δαιδάλλων, περὶ δ᾽ ἄντυγα βάλλε φαεινὴν τρίπλακα μαρμαρέην, ἐκ δ᾽ ἀργύρεον τελαμῶνα.","buckley":"First of all he formed a shield, both large and solid, adorning it all over; and around it he threw a shining border, triple, glittering; and from it suspended a silver belt. Five were the folds of the shield itself; but on it he formed many ornaments with cunning skill.","worldModel":{"vision":"Crucible glow of bronze (28), tin (71), gold (297), and silver (179) ingots against basalt forge walls (72); twenty golden-wheeled tripods.","memory":"Twenty bellows blow into the crucibles by degree as Hephaestus’s work requires; five metallic folds laminate into a single world-surface.","controller":"Hephaestus hammers the five folds on the great anvil while silver-footed Thetis receives the operative world-shield."}}

